@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+id: task-001-spring-newsletter-discount-codes
+type: task
+title: "Spring newsletter discount codes"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Goal
+
+Customers receive discount codes in the newsletter for the spring campaign. An order can take one code, so a customer
+can use it at checkout.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € (500 cents) off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € (3000 cents)
+  or more.
+- An order takes one code at most; a second code replaces the first.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on an order below 30.00 €, is refused with an error that says why. The order is left
+  as it was.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
+- The order book offers `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`.
+- An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus discount
+  plus shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Each code's discount is checked on a worked example, including the half-cent rounding case for `SPRING10`.
+- A `WELCOME5` refusal below 30.00 € and an unknown code are refused with a reason, and the order's totals are unchanged.
+- A replacement code replaces the first, and shipping is the same as without a code.
+- Documented in the public API and in `CHANGELOG.md` under an unreleased heading (no version bump before approval).
